    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Coordinating Committee of the Armed Forces, Police and Territorial Army, fewer than 110 privates, NCOs and junior officers, deposed Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> on 12 September 1974, killed sixty officials of his government on 23 November and abolished the monarchy in March 1975.</li><li>The Red Terror of 1976–1978 killed tens of thousands without trial, by the highest estimates up to 980,000, among them members of the rival Marxist-Leninist EPRP and MEISON; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu Haile Mariam</a>, chairman after the shootout of 3 February 1977, intensified it.</li><li>The famine of 1983–85, which the Derg itself estimated at more than a million deaths, was deliberately worsened in the rebel areas of Tigray and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> as a counter-insurgency strategy, and the regime's enforced resettlement killed between 50,000 and 100,000 more.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Derg was said to have 120 members at its founding in 1974, in fact fewer than 110, and it never admitted a new one; by 1980 expulsions and killings had reduced it to 38, all but three of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amhara">Amhara</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

